# Rank 1515 / CVE-2021-41035: Eclipse OpenJ9 resolved an interface
# method through a method handle without checking the resolved method's
# access flags, so a Java application could invoke a non-public interface
# method and bypass Java access control (execution with unnecessary
# privileges, CWE-250). The dispatch path is three-headed:
# VM_MHInterpreter::dispatchLoop in runtime/vm/MHInterpreter.inc runs
# `method = convertITableIndexToVirtualMethod(receiverClazz,
# interfaceClazz, getVMSlot(methodHandle)); if (NULL != method) { goto
# runMethod; }` with no look at the resolved J9Method's modifiers; the JIT
# counterpart Java_java_lang_invoke_InterfaceHandle_
# convertITableIndexToVTableIndex in runtime/compiler/env/VMJ9.cpp:9496
# returned the itable offset directly; and the JCL wrapper
# InterfaceHandle.java:80 returned `convertITableIndexToVTableIndex(...)
# << VTABLE_ENTRY_SHIFT` unchecked. The fixing merge 9f0b7b785a ("Throw
# IllegalAccessError (IAE): Lookup.findVirtual") carries the three fix
# commits -- VMJ9.cpp now reads the resolved J9Method's modifiers and
# returns -1 when J9AccPublic is absent, MHInterpreter.inc calls
# setIllegalAccessErrorNonPublicInvokeInterface before runMethod, and
# InterfaceHandle.java throws IllegalAccessError on the negative sentinel.
#
# ATTENTION, access-modifier verification vocabulary. The weakness is a
# missing authorization decision on a resolved callee -- no input flows,
# no tainted value reaches a sink, and the two revisions differ only in
# whether the runtime consults the callee's access flags before
# dispatch. Nothing in the corpus can express "this invocation must
# verify the resolved member's accessibility": it is the same
# missing-concept family as ranks 1513/1514 (authorization decisions
# with no dataflow), one step lower in the runtime -- the corpus would
# need a concept for the resolved-method descriptor and a rule judging
# dispatch without an accessibility check. A binding on OpenJ9's own
# convertITableIndexToVirtualMethod or J9AccPublic macros would detect
# this JVM rather than the weakness.
#
# ## Recheck measurements
#
# Re-probed at the recheck span tip, which carries every engine change
# shipped since the first pass. Path 1 does not convert: the auth pack
# still tops out at VYQL-AUTH-178, no concept in the ontology names a
# resolved member's accessibility (the only "visibility"/"non-public"
# hits are content-exposure concepts), and no C++ binding emits
# code.SensitiveOperation, so no later-shipped rule reaches the dispatch.
# Measured 3x --cache off / timeout 180 / --max-ram 6GB per revision on
# the real checkout, vulnerable parent 506de89332 against fix 9f0b7b785a:
#
#   runtime/compiler/env/VMJ9.cpp -- 87/87/87 findings at the parent,
#     88/88/88 at the fix, deterministic; the rule set is identical on
#     both sides (65 VYQL-MEM-006, 13 MEM-002, 5 MEM-016, 4 MEM-004),
#     all memory-family noise, and the +1 is the fix's own added lines
#     shifting an alloca smell. Nothing on the dispatch path.
#   jcl/.../invoke/InterfaceHandle.java -- 0/0/0 at both revisions, and
#     the whole java.lang.invoke package (scanned java:94) reports 0
#     findings at the parent; vyql match on the wrapper labels nothing
#     at all: no source, no sink, no control. The Java half is a hard
#     zero, not a misread one.
#   runtime/vm/MHInterpreter.inc -- "scanned php:1", 0/0/0 at both
#     revisions: .inc routes to the PHP frontend
#     (internal/extract/frontend/registry.go:49), so the interpreter is
#     never parsed as C++. The same bytes under a .cpp name give
#     137/137/137 at both revisions (115 MEM-006 + 22 MEM-016),
#     identical rule sets, so the routing gap is not what blocks the
#     finding: even parsed as C++ nothing discriminates. Re-keying .inc
#     away from PHP would reclassify every .inc in every scan and break
#     the PHP projects that use it for includes, so it is a design call
#     rather than a localized correction, and it would not change this
#     rank's outcome.
#
# The genericity test fails for every binding this fix invites:
# convertITableIndexToVirtualMethod, convertITableIndexToVTableIndex and
# J9AccPublic are OpenJ9-internal names answerable to no library
# documentation, and a generic "native result used without a negative
# sentinel check" rule fires on ordinary JNI wrappers everywhere. No
# definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1515 records the label-free
# dispatch in both languages and the modifier-checked forms, all
# asserting reject VYQL-AUTH-079: when resolved-member accessibility
# lands as vocabulary, the unchecked dispatches must flip to expect.

test "rank1515: the interpreter dispatches a resolved interface method without checking its access flags"
  lang cpp
  file runtime/vm/MHInterpreter_dispatch.cpp
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  static J9Method *dispatchInterfaceMethod(J9VMThread *_currentThread, j9object_t methodHandle, j9object_t receiver) {
      J9Method *method = NULL;
      J9Class *receiverClazz = J9VM_J9CLASS_FROM_HEAPCLASS(_currentThread, receiver);
      J9Class *interfaceClazz = J9VM_J9CLASS_FROM_HEAPCLASS(
          _currentThread, J9VMJAVALANGINVOKEPRIMITIVEHANDLE_REFERENCECLASS(_currentThread, methodHandle));
      method = convertITableIndexToVirtualMethod(receiverClazz, interfaceClazz, getVMSlot(methodHandle));
      if (NULL != method) {
          goto runMethod;
      }
      prepareForExceptionThrow(_currentThread);
      goto throwCurrentException;

  runMethod:
      return method;
  throwCurrentException:
      return NULL;
  }
  ```

test "rank1515: the fixed revision refuses non-public interface methods"
  lang cpp
  file runtime/vm/MHInterpreter_dispatch.cpp
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  static J9Method *dispatchInterfaceMethod(J9VMThread *_currentThread, j9object_t methodHandle, j9object_t receiver) {
      J9Method *method = NULL;
      J9Class *receiverClazz = J9VM_J9CLASS_FROM_HEAPCLASS(_currentThread, receiver);
      J9Class *interfaceClazz = J9VM_J9CLASS_FROM_HEAPCLASS(
          _currentThread, J9VMJAVALANGINVOKEPRIMITIVEHANDLE_REFERENCECLASS(_currentThread, methodHandle));
      method = convertITableIndexToVirtualMethod(receiverClazz, interfaceClazz, getVMSlot(methodHandle));
      if (NULL != method) {
          J9ROMMethod *romMethod = J9_ROM_METHOD_FROM_RAM_METHOD(method);
          if (J9_ARE_NO_BITS_SET(romMethod->modifiers, J9AccPublic)) {
              prepareForExceptionThrow(_currentThread);
              setIllegalAccessErrorNonPublicInvokeInterface(_currentThread, method);
              goto throwCurrentException;
          }
          goto runMethod;
      }
      prepareForExceptionThrow(_currentThread);
      goto throwCurrentException;

  runMethod:
      return method;
  throwCurrentException:
      return NULL;
  }
  ```

test "rank1515: the JCL wrapper returns the itable offset without checking the resolved method"
  lang java
  file jcl/src/java.base/share/classes/java/lang/invoke/InterfaceHandle.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  final class InterfaceHandle extends IndirectHandle {
      protected final long vtableOffset(Object receiver) {
          Class<?> interfaceClass = referenceClass;
          if (interfaceClass.isInstance(receiver)) {
              long interfaceJ9Class = getJ9ClassFromClass(interfaceClass);
              long receiverJ9Class = getJ9ClassFromClass(receiver.getClass());
              return convertITableIndexToVTableIndex(interfaceJ9Class, (int)vmSlot, receiverJ9Class) << VTABLE_ENTRY_SHIFT;
          } else {
              throw new IncompatibleClassChangeError();
          }
      }

      protected static native int convertITableIndexToVTableIndex(long interfaceClass, int itableIndex, long receiverClass);
  }
  ```

test "rank1515: the fixed wrapper throws on the negative sentinel"
  lang java
  file jcl/src/java.base/share/classes/java/lang/invoke/InterfaceHandle.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  final class InterfaceHandle extends IndirectHandle {
      protected final long vtableOffset(Object receiver) {
          Class<?> interfaceClass = referenceClass;
          if (interfaceClass.isInstance(receiver)) {
              long interfaceJ9Class = getJ9ClassFromClass(interfaceClass);
              long receiverJ9Class = getJ9ClassFromClass(receiver.getClass());
              int result = convertITableIndexToVTableIndex(interfaceJ9Class, (int)vmSlot, receiverJ9Class) << VTABLE_ENTRY_SHIFT;
              if (result < 0) {
                  throw new IllegalAccessError();
              }
              return result;
          } else {
              throw new IncompatibleClassChangeError();
          }
      }

      protected static native int convertITableIndexToVTableIndex(long interfaceClass, int itableIndex, long receiverClass);
  }
  ```
